  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "uniequip_001_blackd",
      "name": {
        "en": "Courier's Badge",
        "zh": "讯使证章",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "INITIAL",
      "typeName2": "",
      "icon": "uniequip_001_blackd",
      "description": {
        "en": "Operator Courier has demonstrated a remarkable aptitude for preemptive penetration of the battlefield situation and active offense so as to secure leeway for deployment.\nThe Field Operations Department has thus passed the following resolution:\nThis operator shall hereby be appointed a Vanguard Operator during field operations to exercise Pioneer responsibilities.\nIn witness whereof,\nThis badge is hereby conferred upon the above named.",
        "zh": "干员讯使擅长抢先切入战局，通过进攻争取部署空间\n根据外勤部门决议\n在外勤任务中划分为先锋干员，行使尖兵职责\n特别颁发此证章\n以兹证明",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "uniequip_002_blackd",
      "name": {
        "en": "Low Temperature Resistant Communication Equipment",
        "zh": "耐低温通讯设备",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "ADVANCED",
      "typeName2": "X",
      "icon": "uniequip_002_blackd",
      "description": {
        "en": "Weiss brushes the snow off his body, and enters.\nIf it weren't for the bandages and bruises, you would never suspect from his unrelenting faint smile that he'd just gone through bitter hell.\nIt was an attempt on Enciodes's life. Comms were cut off before Weiss could state the precise location, leaving Enciodes's guards no choice but to provisionally surround him. Shields and blades firm in hand, they noted, out of the corners of their eyes, the Caprinae woman standing by their master's side.\nThey were all sure that with this Caprinae bodyguard by his side, no attempt would ever succeed. They just needed to coordinate with each other and settle this chaos while keeping casualties to a minimum. Not to mention, Weiss managed to get the most critical part of the message out, so now all they had to do was wait patiently for the enemy to serve themselves up.\nBut they didn't get to await the enemy.\nIn fact, when they caught sight of the traps on the mountain that had taken down a dozen or so of said enemy, the guards, shields and blades and all, were momentarily shocked—just a few branches hidden in the snow, plus flint blades fashioned out of rocks struck together, formed traps no one would ever notice and yet which sunk circle after circle of blood into the white snow, a faintly sanguine pink even leeching into the tundra some meters out.\nAnd strewn all along the tundra were the enemy's now frozen severed limbs, as well as blood and pulped flesh hacked free from Weiss himself, forming mound upon mound in the snowfall. Sunk into the dismembered parts were wounds fierce, firm, and even visibly wrathful, while the cuts on Weiss that bared bone made every guard wince.\nItra do not reign supreme in sturdiness, and though Weiss's abilities excel, he is only human. Only a single member of Enciodes's guards, one who spends a considerable amount of time merely couriering Kjerag's letters to boot. People are fond of the faint scent on the letters he handles, and of his cheery face, and they admire his loyalty to Enciodes.\nBut no one would've imagined he had this side to him too.\nWhy? Nobody had asked Weiss to go so far. Being all on his own, simply passing on the word would've sufficed. He could've found somewhere to hide, and mustered enough defense to cope with this spate of traitors.\nEnciodes looks over Weiss, but makes no move to ask him anything. Weiss sorts out the letters and documents on the table and deferentially excuses himself. Before the door closes, Enciodes hears a cut-off remark vanish into the wind: '...live up to duty.'",
        "zh": "魏斯掸干净身上的落雪，走进屋里。\n如果不是身上的绷带和伤痕，在他仍旧有着淡淡笑容的脸上，丝毫看不出这个人刚刚经历过一番苦战。\n那是一场针对恩希欧迪斯的刺杀。通讯在魏斯说出具体地点之前被掐断，护卫们只好暂时守卫在恩希欧迪斯周围。他们攥紧盾和刀，余光确认着那个站在老爷身边的卡普里尼女人。 \n护卫们确信，只要这位卡普里尼护卫在老爷身旁，一切刺杀都不会得逞。他们只需互相配合，就能在将伤亡压到最小的情况下平息这场混乱。更何况，魏斯已经传出最重要的信息，那么，他们接下来要做的就是耐心地等敌人前来送死。 \n但他们并没有等来敌人。 \n并且在山上看到那个分解了十数个敌人的陷阱时，这些手握刀盾的护卫们短暂地震惊了——仅仅只是一些掩藏在落雪中的树枝，和由石头相击而临时制成的锋利石片，这个原本不会被人注意到的陷阱所漫出的血浸透了四周一圈又一圈的白雪，甚至在几米外的雪地都有着血液被稀释后的淡淡粉色。\n雪地一路上还散落着敌人已经僵硬的肢体残块，以及魏斯本人的鲜血和被斩伤脱离开身体的碎肉，在落雪中堆成了一个又一个雪包。肢体残块上的刀口狠、稳，甚至能看出其中夹杂的怒火，而魏斯身上那些深可见骨的刀口，也让护卫们不禁皱起眉头。\n依特拉并不是一个十分强壮的种族，魏斯即使有着过人的能力，也不过是一人，不过是恩希欧迪斯身边一个小小的护卫，甚至他平时有相当一部分的时间只是在为谢拉格传递信件。人们喜欢从他手里接过带着淡淡香味的信，喜欢他开朗的面庞，也欣赏他对恩希欧迪斯的忠心。\n但人们没有想到他还有这样的一面。\n为什么呢？并没有人要求魏斯做到这一步，传递消息对于孤身一人的他来说已经足够，他大可以寻找一个地方隐藏起来，有足够的护卫能够应对这次反叛。\n恩希欧迪斯看着眼前的魏斯，并没有开口问什么。魏斯整理好桌面上的信件和文书，恭敬地退下。在门关上前，恩希欧迪斯听到了消散在风中的半句话：“……不辱使命。”",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ],
